## Environment notes for the next session

- `~/.local/bin` was EMPTY at session start. Rebuilt there: `buildlock`,
  `autocheckpoint`, `render-md-pdf`, `milestone-bars`. These survive reboot.
- **`buildlock` must use `flock -o`** — the `exec 9>` form leaks the lock fd to
  every child, and a harness process held it for 15 minutes this morning while
  every build queued silently behind it.
- The sandbox battery needs host provisioning exactly as
  `.github/actions/host-sandbox-setup/action.yml` does it (global git identity,
  `~/.ssh/known_hosts`, `~/.ssh/id_ed25519`). Without it 36 tests fail for
  environmental reasons. It is provisioned now.
- **Do not give parallel lanes a shared `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`** — a stale
  integration-test binary bakes in its manifest path and lanes fail with a
  file-not-found pointing nowhere useful. Cost three builds today.
- `failure-atlas` MCP is still NOT registered, so every mutation proof today was
  hand-rolled. The other Claude session has the infra prompt at
  `design-docs/handoffs/2026-08-30-other-claude-infra-lane.md`.
- Another Claude session and codex share this box. The other session rewrote
  `~/.ssh/` twice this morning and broke the gate both times.

